WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.819
This September, get ready for a whole new
round of great Netflix programming.

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:09.610
Headlining the month is Maniac, which stars
Jonah Hill and Emma Stone as two participants

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.410
in a medical study that goes disastrously
wrong.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:17.790
Other highlights include new seasons of Netflix
originals Iron Fist and American Vandal, along

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.380
with the original film Hold the Dark.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.740
In fact, there's so much heading to Netflix
in September that it's hard to keep track

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.660
of everything, so we've rounded up the best
new releases to look forward to next month.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.359
"Let's get down to the nitty gritty."

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:35.540
Here's everything good coming to Netflix in
September 2018.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.940
Atypical: Season 2

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.899
Critics and audiences loved the first season
of Atypical, which follows a high schooler

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:47.329
on the autism spectrum as he does his best
to navigate school and family life.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:52.261
With comedy and drama in equal measure, Atypical
was quick to draw in a loyal fan base, and

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:57.020
Kier Gilchrist in particular delivered a winning
performance as the main character, Sam.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.180
Season 2 will pick up right where the first
season left off, following Sam's dysfunctional

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.910
family as they deal with their particular
brand of atypical drama.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.120
Look for it on September 7th.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.800
Marvel's Iron Fist: Season 2

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.590
Even though Iron Fist has the unfortunate
legacy of being the least-liked Marvel show

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.500
on Netflix so far, that hasn't stopped the
character from making an impact.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.750
Iron Fist showed up in the team-up series
The Defenders, and now he's back with a second

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.620
season of his standalone show.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.960
"You back for more?"

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.160
"Oh, we've not even started."

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:34.430
Will the new season manage to rise above the
rocky foundations laid out in its first outing?

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.470
Find out when Iron Fist returns on September
7th.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.740
American Vandal: Season 2

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.140
We didn't think it was possible, but American
Vandal is getting even more meta in Season

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.140
2.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.640
In the first season, the show revolved around
a vandal who defaced a school.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.290
In Season 2, someone named the Turd Burglar
is spiking the cafeteria food.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.720
But the line is blurring between fact and
fiction.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.560
From scenes of their own show on Netflix to
emails between Netflix and the made-up documentarians

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.530
who "investigated" the original crimes, American
Vandal Season 2 is plunging so deep into parody

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:08.360
that it's even mocking itself.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.000
Get caught up in the mystery on September
14th.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.470
BoJack Horseman: Season 5

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:18.500
For four seasons of horseplay and nihilism,
BoJack Horseman has alternately stunned, broken,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.860
and uplifted audiences.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.480
The story of a has-been sitcom star who's
still trying to chase the dream in Hollywood,

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:28.520
it's the kind of show that plays like a comedy,
only to sneak up on you with pain and sadness.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.560
"One drink."

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.260
What can we expect when Season 5 lands?

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.900
Honestly, with BoJack Horseman there's no
telling, so we'll all have until September

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.380
14th to find out.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.640
Maniac: Limited Series

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.340
Netflix has been dropping teasers for Maniac
for months now, and we're still not entirely

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.030
sure what the series is about.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:53.240
The premise is no secret: Jonah Hill and Emma
Stone are two strangers who take part in a

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.640
pharmaceutical trial.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.480
After that, all bets are off as the trailers
dive into a montage of paranoia and alternate

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:00.480
realities.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.240
We do know that Cary Fukunaga, the mastermind
behind True Detective and the screenwriter

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:10.350
of It, is helming the series, which promises
a dark journey into the human psyche.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:12.920
Check it out on September 21st.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:13.920
Quincy

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:19.160
Rashida Jones rose to fame as Ann Perkins
on Parks and Recreation in 2009, and she's

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.000
been going nonstop ever since.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.480
"Ann Perkins!"

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.400
"Aaaaaaaan Perkins!"

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:29.240
The actress is the daughter of legendary musician
and producer Quincy Jones, and now Rashida

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:32.069
is turning her sights on dear old dad with
Quincy.

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:36.720
The documentary will offer an intimate look
at Quincy Jones' professional career and his

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.720
private life.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.060
Take a look on September 21st.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.480
The Good Cop

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.400
Netflix's upcoming series The Good Cop marks
the streaming service's first foray into procedural

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.340
crime shows anchored by quirky, off-kilter
detectives.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:55.340
The series stars Tony Danza and Josh Groban
as a father and son, both of whom are NYPD

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.340
cops.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.080
Well, the father used to be, at least - until
he was kicked off the force and sent to jail

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.080
for seven years.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:05.610
Now, his son is a straight-laced, by-the-book
detective who's trying hard to stay away from

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.030
the corruption that landed his dad behind
bars.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.010
"I taught him everything I know."

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.290
"Except right from wrong."

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.880
Look for it on September 21st.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.880
Norsemen: Season 2

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:20.100
On the surface, Norsemen looks like a spoof
of shows like Vikings and Game of Thrones,

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.190
but watch a little longer and you'll find
so much more than that.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:27.850
Norsemen anchors its many jokes with its own
characters, storylines, and surprisingly rich

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.280
production design.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.240
"Farewell brother."

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.400
"Why don't you just let me do it, because
I…"

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.910
"No, no, it's just my hands are very cold."

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:42.680
It's not a comedy style for everyone, but
with Season 2 heading for Netflix on September

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.650
26th, you'll have plenty of time to give Norsemen
a chance.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:48.760
"You have something that belongs to me."

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.080
"We're actually in control here, so…"

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.620
Hold the Dark

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.950
From Jeremy Saulnier, the director of Blue
Ruin and Green Room, Hold the Dark is about

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:04.260
a writer who's summoned to Alaska to track
down the wolves that carried off a woman's

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.260
son.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.639
Once he starts digging into the case, though,
he finds that there's more to the story than

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:09.830
he'd realized.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:14.760
Westworld's Jeffrey Wright stars alongside
Alexander Skarsgard and Riley Keough.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.540
Look for Hold the Dark to hit Netflix on September
28th.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.590
New original standup

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:25.050
Netflix always has a few treats for stand-up
comedy fans, and September is no different.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.940
On the 11th, look for Daniel Sloss: Live Shows.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.050
The Scottish comedian will be hitting on a
range of controversial topics with his trademark

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.180
humor style.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.830
On the 18th, look for D.L.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:38.400
Hughley in an all-new Netflix special entitled
Contrarian.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.520
With everything from Black Panther to current
politics on the table, it's bound to be an

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.410
entertaining show.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.430
New movies

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:50.260
This September, you'll get the chance to explore
the high seas, battle for evil ex supremacy,

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:54.449
and take a walk on the wild side - and you
can do it all without ever leaving the couch.

00:05:54.449 --> 00:05:59.949
On September 1st, check out action favorites
like Spider-Man 3, King Kong, and Pearl Harbor.

00:05:59.949 --> 00:06:05.080
Then, look for Black Panther on the 4th, Scott
Pilgrim vs. the World on the 16th, and Pirates

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.150
of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl
on the 25th.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:12.550
If watching Topher Grace lose his mind to
an alien symbiote in Spider-Man 3 doesn't

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:17.419
do it for you, you can also watch him lose
his mind in a haunted house with the 2018

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:18.510
thriller Delirium.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:25.230
"Ooh my spider sense is tingling, if you know
what I'm talking about."

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:29.420
Delirium arrives on the first, side-by-side
with screamers like Stephanie, The Keeping

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.780
Hours, and The Texas Chainsaw Massacre: The
Beginning.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:38.380
And on the 17th, make sure you tune in for
The Witch, 2016's most terrifying movie about

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.380
Puritans.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.120
There won't be a lot of new drama films heading
to Netflix in September, but the few that

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.530
are are definite winners.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:48.961
In particular, be sure to look for Scarface,
Unforgiven, and The Cider House Rules, the

00:06:48.961 --> 00:06:51.800
Oscar-winning drama about a World War II orphanage.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:54.240
"I hate orphans."

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.640
"Say it again to my face!"

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.550
"I hate them!"

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:01.389
If you're looking for something lighter, the
first of the month sees a handful of comedies

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:03.100
joining the Netflix ranks.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:07.710
You'll get classics like Groundhog Day right
alongside modern favorites like Bruce Almighty,

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:11.590
The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, and
Nacho Libre.

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:12.960
New television

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.870
Netflix's television selection is ratcheting
up the horror this month.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:21.720
The biggest new addition is American Horror
Story: Cult, which is hitting Netflix on September

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:22.720
18.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:26.979
Earlier in the month, you can also dig into
Season 3 of Quantico on the 2nd, Season 2

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:31.250
of Van Helsing on the 5th, and Season 7 of
Once Upon a Time on the 6th.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:36.370
Finally, grab your wire-wrapped baseball bat
replica, or whatever, and settle in for Season

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.419
8 of The Walking Dead on the 23rd.

00:07:38.419 --> 00:07:43.260
"Ha ha ha, easy peasy lemon squeezy!"

